      "Language": "pol",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We present the case of a woman treated with coronary angioplasty due to non-ST segment elevation myocardial infarction,then again because of restenosis, who continued to complain of chest pain and syncope. Holter electrocardiogram recording revealed atrioventricular block related to ST-segment elevations and variant angina was diagnosed. Despite administered medications, the patient required pacemaker implantation."},
